              {
                "title": "Q1665 (Nov. 14, 2025)",
                "question": "Do I need to declare the exact name of the card?",
                "answer": "No. As long as you and your opponent(s) mutually understand which card you mean, there is no need to recite the exact name of the card.\n\nAdditionally, if you forget the name of a card during an official tournament or event, you may ask a judge for assistance in remembering, provided you abide by said tournament or event's rules."
              },
              {
                "title": "Q1664 (Nov. 14, 2025)",
                "question": "Can I declare the name of a token card, such as Fairy?",
                "answer": "Yes, you can."
              },
              {
                "title": "Q1663 (Nov. 14, 2025)",
                "question": "Can I declare a collab card's alternate name like Lelouch, Leader of the Black Knights?",
                "answer": "No. An alternate name isn't a card name. However, if you declare Demonlord Eachtar, then reveal Lelouch, you would draw 2 cards, since Lelouch has the card name Demonlord Eachtar."
              },
              {
                "title": "Q1662 (Nov. 14, 2025)",
                "question": "If the card I reveal is not the card I declared, is the 1 card I draw the same card I revealed?",
                "answer": "Yes, that's correct. If you declared correctly, the 2 cards you draw would be the revealed card and 1 more."
              }
            ],
